{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/research_history/episode11_build_round10.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport hashlib,json\nroot=Path('/tmp/research_history');base=(root/'683_episode11_class_centered_residual_geometry_zero_start/method.py').read_text();entries=[]\ndef save(num,name,src,h):\n d=root/(str(num)+'_episode11_'+name);d.mkdir(exist_ok=True);(d/'method.py').write_text(src)\n entries.append({'name':d.name,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(src.encode()).hexdigest(),'hypothesis':h})\na=base.index('    f=torch.where(amask,asq+bsq.sum(1)');b=base.index('    K=None;shift=None;rs=None;cs=None',a)\nnew='''    Ac=A-amean[:,None,:];Bc=B-bmean[:,None,:]\n    C=torch.bmm(Bc,Ac.transpose(1,2)).transpose(1,2).mul_(-1.)\n    offset=(amean*bmean).sum(1)-asq.sum(1)/an-bsq.sum(1)/bn\n    unary_mean=-2*offset\n    C.add_(offset[:,None,None])\n    C.masked_fill_(~(amask[:,:,None] & bmask[:,None,:]),float('inf'))\n    initial_bound=float((-C.amin((1,2))/etable[2]).max())\n    f=torch.zeros((100,nmax));g=torch.zeros((100,mmax))\n'''\ns=base[:a]+new+base[b:]\nsave(684,'class_centered_geometry_no_initial_duals',s,'Obtain the removed unary mean from the centered geometry offset; start zero duals directly and guard the actual residual exponent range.')\n# Center unique supports before packing, reusing twenty empirical means and squared-norm means.\na=s.index('    for i,a in enumerate(aa):A[i*10:');b=s.index('    def direct(f,g,eps):',a)\nnew='''    ua=torch.stack([a.mean(0) for a in aa]);ub=torch.stack([b.mean(0) for b in bb])\n    un=torch.stack([a.square().sum(1).mean()/2 for a in aa]);vn=torch.stack([b.square().sum(1).mean()/2 for b in bb])\n    for i,a in enumerate(aa):A[i*10:(i+1)*10,:len(a)]=a-ua[i]\n    for j,b in enumerate(bb):B[j::10,:len(b)]=b-ub[j]\n    amask = torch.arange(nmax)[None,:] < an[:,None]\n    bmask = torch.arange(mmax)[None,:] < bn[:,None]\n    C=torch.bmm(B,A.transpose(1,2)).transpose(1,2).mul_(-1.)\n    offset=((ua @ ub.T)-un[:,None]-vn[None,:]).flatten()\n    unary_mean=-2*offset\n    C.add_(offset[:,None,None])\n    C.masked_fill_(~(amask[:,:,None] & bmask[:,None,:]),float('inf'))\n    initial_bound=float((-C.amin((1,2))/etable[2]).max())\n    la=(1/an.float()).log()[:,None];lb=(1/bn.float()).log()[:,None]\n'''\ns2=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\na2=s2.index('    amean=A.sum(1)/an[:,None]');b2=s2.index('    K=None;shift=None;rs=None;cs=None',a2)\ns2=s2[:a2]+'''    f=torch.zeros((100,nmax));g=torch.zeros((100,mmax))\n'''+s2[b2:]\nsave(685,'class_unique_centered_geometry',s2,'Center twenty unique empirical supports before packing; compute pair offsets from twenty norms and a 10x10 mean-dot matrix.')\n# Combine with the point recurrence/GEMM candidate under current complete evaluation.\ns3=(root/'671_episode11_point_gemm_columns_point_recurrence_residual_increments/method.py').read_text();pa=s3.index('def _dual');pb=s3.index('def _label_cost')\nsave(686,'class_unique_centered_point_increments_gemm',s2[:s2.index('def _dual')]+s3[pa:pb]+s2[s2.index('def _label_cost'):],'Combine unique centered class geometry with exact point residual increments and column GEMM reductions.')\n(root/'episode11_round10_manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(entries,indent=2));print(json.dumps(entries,indent=2))\nPY\npython /tmp/research_history/episode11_build_round10.py\ncat >> /tmp/research_history/episode11_derivations.md <<'MD'\n\n## Direct centered class residual geometry\nInitial class duals are f0_i=||a_i||²/2 + E||b||²/2 - a_i dot E(b), and similarly g0_j. Therefore R0=C-f0-g0 = -(a_i-Ea) dot (b_j-Eb) + Ea dot Eb - E||a||²/2 - E||b||²/2. The scalar offset is negative mean(C). Solve using R0 and zero initial duals, then restore mean(f0)+mean(g0)=2mean(C) to the pair objective. Computing the centered product skips original dense unary costs and first-stage subtraction. Original-temperature geometry and masks remain. A control forms the gauge via original geometry before subtraction; another centers the twenty unique supports once before packing and derives offsets from their unique means/norms. The first unshifted exponential is allowed only if the actual maximum residual exponent is below60, with original stable shifted fallback otherwise.\nMD\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
